  "configuration_id": "config_003",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_006: scgpt + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted → 52.0% acc), we have very sparse evidence and high uncertainty about which architectural choices are driving performance. The most informative next step is a clean single-variable ablation: config_003 changes only the aggregation from transformer to avgpool while keeping the same RNA encoder (scgpt), image encoder (imagenet_vit_l), profile setting (multiprofile), and fusion (weighted). This directly tests whether the more complex transformer aggregation is actually contributing meaningful gain over a simpler average-pooling strategy, or whether it is overfitting/underperforming. If avgpool matches or exceeds transformer, we can eliminate the transformer branch from further exploration and redirect remaining budget toward encoder and fusion choices. If transformer clearly wins, we gain confidence to build on that architecture. This is the best use of experiment 2 because it isolates one critical design variable with a direct comparison to our only data point, maximizing information gain per experiment under the 10-experiment budget."
}

